{"t":"2026-09-25T06:39:35.546Z","mode":"turns","direction":"daemon->client","payload":{"id":1,"result":{"data":[{"id":"01a0d746-ea41-77e1-bea6-cb9e4d29e192","items":[{"type":"userMessage","id":"01a0d746-eaed-7512-87a7-f68f6879075b","clientId":"1807dd40-d34b-4796-9516-84e3d35f8077","content":[{"type":"text","text":"G2 spike queued message (sent via thread/queue/add while the previous turn was still running): after finishing, reply with exactly the words OAC G2 QUEUED.","text_elements":[]}]},{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0abacd31cf7459ca016ab6163f6af887d183cae4608933872e","summary":[],"content":[]},{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0abacd31cf7459ca016ab6163f8fd487d1986fbe05a3754c81","text":"OAC G2 QUEUED","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null,"questions":null}],"itemsView":"full","status":"completed","error":null,"startedAt":1790318144,"completedAt":1790318145,"durationMs":1559},{"id":"01a0d746-b85a-7b71-868a-51b95a053b43","items":[{"type":"userMessage","id":"01a0d746-b8d3-7e12-99ee-1c139eb206ed","clientId":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"G2 spike busy-turn test: write a numbered list of 40 distinct one-sentence facts about lighthouses. Do not use any tools.","text_elements":[]}]},{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0abacd31cf7459ca016ab61633838c87d1b8736f894642cd1b","summary":[],"content":[]},{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0abacd31cf7459ca016ab6163432b487d191f8ea9fd34c711d","text":"1. Lighthouses are towers or structures that emit light to help guide ships.\n2. Many lighthouses are built near rocky coastlines.\n3. Lighthouse beams can warn mariners about reefs and shoals.\n4. Fresnel lenses focus light into powerful beams.\n5. Augustin-Jean Fresnel developed the modern lighthouse lens.\n6. Some lighthouse beams rotate to create distinctive patterns.\n7. Flashing patterns help sailors identify individual lighthouses.\n8. Lighthouses often have distinctive colors or markings for daytime recognition.\n9. Lighthouse keepers historically maintained lamps and lenses.\n10. Many lighthouse keepers lived in attached keeper’s cottages.\n11. Early lighthouses commonly burned oil or whale oil.\n12. Modern lighthouses usually use electric lamps.\n13. Some remote lighthouses use solar panels for power.\n14. Lighthouse foghorns provide warnings when visibility is poor.\n15. Fog signals can have distinct sound patterns.\n16. The Lighthouse of Alexandria was one of the ancient world’s famous landmarks.\n17. The Lighthouse of Alexandria stood on the island of Pharos.\n18. Many historic lighthouses have spiral staircases.\n19. Lighthouse towers are often tapered to withstand strong winds.\n20. Thick masonry walls help some lighthouses resist waves and storms.\n21. Offshore lighthouses may be built on submerged rocks.\n22. Some lighthouses are mounted on offshore platforms.\n23. Lightships served as floating lighthouse stations.\n24. Buoys can supplement the warnings provided by lighthouses.\n25. Lighthouse locations are recorded on nautical charts.\n26. Mariners can use lighthouse bearings to determine their positions.\n27. Automated systems have replaced many resident lighthouse keepers.\n28. Some lighthouses are preserved as museums.\n29. Lighthouse lantern rooms are usually located at the top of the tower.\n30. A lighthouse’s light characteristic describes its timing pattern.\n31. Different colored sectors can indicate safe or dangerous directions.\n32. Red sectors often mark hazards in navigational lighting systems.\n33. White light generally indicates a navigationally safer sector.\n34. Lighthouses can help vessels navigate harbor entrances.\n35. Some lighthouses mark river mouths.\n36. Lighthouse foundations must be engineered for local geology and wave conditions.\n37. Brick, stone, concrete, and steel have all been used to build lighthouses.\n38. Lighthouse lenses require regular cleaning to maintain brightness.\n39. Many lighthouses have become symbols of coastal communities.\n40. Lighthouses continue to serve as aids to navigation despite satellite systems.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null,"questions":null}],"itemsView":"full","status":"completed","error":null,"startedAt":1790318131,"completedAt":1790318144,"durationMs":12750},{"id":"01a0d745-d414-71c1-a9cc-9f2c975bf23c","items":[{"type":"userMessage","id":"01a0d745-d62e-7920-96ca-814073eec2f1","clientId":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"G2 spike test (from a second client of the local daemon, not typed in this TUI): reply with exactly the words OAC G2 RECEIVED.","text_elements":[]}]},{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0abacd31cf7459ca016ab615f8b71487d1a6fc4ae8b48774fb","summary":[],"content":[]},{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0abacd31cf7459ca016ab615f8e98487d194abefcc7ffa3a98","text":"OAC G2 RECEIVED","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null,"questions":null}],"itemsView":"full","status":"completed","error":null,"startedAt":1790318072,"completedAt":1790318074,"durationMs":2111},{"id":"01a0d744-ad00-78f0-a693-939cc2a1fcb1","items":[{"type":"userMessage","id":"01a0d744-b2f4-7c31-9c0c-e9712e877bdb","clientId":"1850d398-4a04-43e2-9c3b-0625dd5fbfed","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Greet me in one word.","text_elements":[]}]},{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0abacd31cf7459ca016ab615ae29dc87d1b547170724783001","text":"Hello","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null,"questions":null}],"itemsView":"full","status":"completed","error":null,"startedAt":1790317997,"completedAt":1790318000,"durationMs":2902}],"nextCursor":null,"backwardsCursor":"{\"requestedThreadId\":\"01a0d743-f182-7120-b2b6-9238a6d06e06\",\"rolloutOrdinal\":35,\"includeAnchor\":true,\"scope\":{\"kind\":\"turns\"}}"}}}
